  "notes": [
    "Parameters are learned control hypotheses, not measured biological physiology.",
    "The default eight-second episode requires grounded takeoff, sustained powered flight, and stable foot-supported landing. Posture alone earns no positive reward.",
    "Odor, taste and body feedback remain active. The observer preview is not retinal input.",
    "The 27-parameter search fits power, deployment time, frequency, and separate mean-angle/amplitude gains for 12 steering muscle types. Bilateral homologues share gains but receive separate muscle forces. BANC physiology, synapses, sensory transduction, muscle dynamics, other limb mappings, native aerodynamics and wingbeat tables stay fixed.",
    "Reward and task stage never enter the motor decoder. Flight thresholds are declared modeling criteria.",
    "Contributor returns are unverified; a changed objective requires a new coordinator run and independent evaluation.",
    "Objective criteria v3: physical failures retain measured takeoff, controlled airtime and landing progress with one constant penalty. Terminal crash severity does not rank equal-progress trials. Qualification, full horizons and invalid/external-force rejection stay fixed."
  ]
